# Docker

<Aside title="Placeholder">

This page is a stub. The published image reference, a compose example, and the recommended way to pass secrets are still being written.

</Aside>

Running the server in Docker is mostly a matter of passing the same environment the binary reads. The container is stateless: it holds no database and no artifacts, so both must be external.

At minimum you will set:

- `APP_ENV=production` (or `staging`).
- The database variables from [Database](/self-hosting/database/), pointing at a Postgres you run.
- The storage variables from [Storage](/self-hosting/storage/), pointing at a bucket.
- `WYRD_SIGNING_KEY_FILE` mounted as a secret, per [Authentication](/self-hosting/authentication/).

Full image name, tags, and a worked compose file will land here.

